course: dictionary
lesson: 15599
title: Tailor: a person and a verb
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A tailor is a person whose job is to make, mend or change clothes, especially suits and coats. «My grandad is a tailor, and he sews suits for people in our town.» The words around tailor tell you it is a job, because grandad sews suits.
explain: Tailor can also be a verb, a doing word. To tailor clothes is to make them fit a person exactly. «The tailor measured my arm so the new coat would fit.» Measuring the arm is a clue that the tailor is making the coat fit well.
explain: Tailor can also mean to make something suit a special need. «Each child had a plan tailored to their own needs.» Tailored here does not mean sewn. It means the plan was made to suit each child. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: «Each child had a plan made to suit their own needs.» That still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: A tailor is a person who makes, mends or changes clothes.
fact: Tailors often make suits and coats, and they measure people carefully so the clothes fit.
fact: «Tailor-made» means made just for you, to fit you exactly.
fact: Tailor is also a verb. Tailors, tailored and tailoring are the other forms of this word.
fact: In «The Emperor's New Clothes» and «The Brave Little Tailor», a tailor is a character in the story, so the word can appear in stories as well as in real life.
exercise: «My grandad is a tailor who sews suits for people in town.» What is a tailor? | A person who drives a bus | A person who sells fish at the market | A kind of sharp pair of scissors | *A person who makes or mends clothes
exercise: «Each child had a plan tailored to their own needs.» What does tailored mean here? | *Made to suit each child's needs | Copied from a book | Written in pencil | Very long and boring
exercise: «The tailor measured my arm so the new coat would fit.» Find and copy the word that tells you the tailor checked the size. | *measured | coat | would | arm
test: Ruby says «tailor-made» means made for nobody else. What does tailor-made mean? | Made out of paper | *Made just for you | Made in a factory for everyone | Made by a robot
test: Which word is a verb in «She will tailor the dress for the school play»? | school | dress | *tailor | play
exam: Which sentence uses tailor as a verb? | *She will tailor the dress to fit the bride | The tailor sold him a new coat | My tailor lives on our street | The tailors had a shop in the town
